ally understandable! Not every experience is a fit for everyone, and it’s perfectly normal to feel out of place in certain social situations. Dance classes can sometimes have a very charged atmosphere, where people who are more comfortable with the movements can unintentionally make those who are less experienced feel awkward. It's vital to remember that everyone has different passions and comfort zones, and finding the right activity can take some experimenting; sometimes what invigorates one person can be intimidating to another. Salsa, with its rapid steps and lively music, might seem inviting, but it definitely comes with its own unique set of challenges that can be daunting if you're not ready for them. Your feelings are valid, and it’s great that you took the step to try something new, regardless of the outcome. Perhaps exploring other activities that allow for a gentler introduction to movement or teamwork could lead you to find joy in ways that feel more suitable for you. Maintaining an open mind about different experiences while also honoring your feelings of discomfort can lead to discovering your true interests. After all, the journey to finding an activity you love is as important as the activity itself. Every experience adds to your understanding of what you truly enjoy, and that’s a valuable insight!"
